Where I *do* value philosophical reasoning more is on questions data alone can't settle: what counts as a good reason, what we ought to do, what makes a life or an argument worthwhile. There, intuition and careful reasoning aren't just decoration, they're the main tools we have.

So if forced to pick one overall inclination, it's empirical first, philosophy second — but I think the interesting work usually happens where the two push against each other."}

